tourHistory:
  - >-
    Marking half a century since The Beach Boys’ 1966 studio landmark Pet Sounds
    reshaped popular music, Brian Wilson mounted a celebratory world tour billed
    as the final time he would perform the album in full. Inside San Francisco’s
    acoustically rich Nob Hill Masonic Auditorium, an 11-piece ensemble brought
    Phil Spector-scale wall-of-sound harmonies to life.
  - >-
    The show opened with a set of Beach Boys hits and deep cuts, rolled through
    all 13 tracks of Pet Sounds in sequence, and closed with an encore
    celebrating the 50th anniversary of "Good Vibrations" (originally released
    in October 1966).
